   "resumo_en": "Dose is the second studio album by American rock band Gov't Mule. It was released on February 24, 1998, by Capricorn Records and (on vinyl) by Evil Teen Records. It was produced, recorded and mixed by Michael Barbiero and is a much darker record than Gov't Mule's self-titled debut album. The songs \"Thelonius Beck\" and \"Birth of the Mule\" were tributes to jazz musicians Thelonious Monk and Miles Davis, respectively, whereas the subtitle \"Beck\" refers to Jeff Beck, who also recorded a song named \"Thelonius\".",
